.TH XMR\-KEYS 1 2026-10-25 "blocktools 0.1.0" "blocktools manual"
.SH NAME
xmr\-keys \- xmr\-keys [\-\-net main|stage|test] [\-\-scan\-out FILE [\-\-restore\-height N]] < seed
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
{"error":"monero_seed_needs_25_words"}
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
stdout: one JSON line of PUBLIC data (address, public spend/view keys).
\-\-scan\-out writes a monero\-wallet\-rpc `generate_from_keys` request for a VIEW\-ONLY wallet
(address + private view key, no spend key) to FILE, created new with mode 0600. The view key
is secret (it reveals incoming funds), so it never goes to stdout or stderr.
.SH OPTIONS
See SYNOPSIS; this tool has no separate long\-option list beyond \-\-help.
.SH INPUT/OUTPUT
stdout: one JSON line of PUBLIC data (address, public spend/view keys).
is secret (it reveals incoming funds), so it never goes to stdout or stderr.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
0
Success (JSON lines may still carry status fields such as done / no_candidates).
.TP
2
Bad input, unsupported shape, or tool\-reported failure (JSON status is the detail).
.TP
3
Refused on purpose (watch\-only, policy deny, human abort, missing confirmation).
.PP
Other nonzero codes are tool\-specific; always read the last JSON status line.
.SH EXAMPLES
.nf
See recipes/ for end\-to\-end flows. Search for xmr\-keys in recipes/*.md.
| monero_seed | xmr\-keys address, exit 3 \-> xmr\-wallet (host) | monero.md |
.fi
.SH SECURITY NOTES
DANGEROUS: audit before use with real funds. See docs/SECURITY.md.
Run secret\-touching tools only inside ./blocktools run (sealed, offline).
.SH SEE ALSO
blocktools(7), docs/SECURITY.md, docs/getting\-started.md, recipes/README.md
